COMMUNICATION AND PUBLIC RELATIONS OFFICE
Senior Officer / Officer (26270056)
The Communication and Public Relations Office is seeking a self-motivated individual to support and drive the University’s corporate communications and public relations initiatives.
Responsibilities:
Organise and implement media publicity initiatives to elevate the University’s profile;
Proactively identify and develop newsworthy stories to enhance positive media exposure for the University;
Draft, edit, and manage a range of publicity materials and content for distribution across internal and external communication platforms;
Assist in handling media enquiries and responding to requests in a timely manner;
Monitor media channels for coverage concerning the University and prepare regular summaries as required;
Develop and maintain strong working relationships with internal and external stakeholders; and
Support the Office in various functional areas and perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor.
Requirements:
A recognised degree, preferably in Journalism, Communication Studies, or a related discipline, with a proven ability to work effectively as part of a team;
At least five years of relevant work experience in corporate communications, public affairs and media relations;
Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, with demonstrated creativity and ability to produce compelling and impactful content;
Experience in networking and building relationships with media professionals;
Strong sensitivity in current affairs and political landscape;
Detail-oriented, highly organised, and capable of working independently with strong project management skills;
Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills; and
Willingness to work on weekends and outside office hours when required.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written assessment.
Candidates with less experience will be considered for appointment as Officer.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of two years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to performance review and mutual agreement.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
