FACULTY OF ARTS & SOCIAL SCIENCES
ACADEMY OF GEOGRAPHY, SOCIOLOGY AND INTERNATIONAL STUDIES
Research Assistant (26270107)
The Academy of Geography, Sociology and International Studies, would like to seek applicants for Research Assistant with a strong interest in researching tourism and Chinese nationalism.
Responsibilities:
Work with the Principal Investigator on the research projects related to tourism and Chinese nationalism;
Analyse online source material using Little Red Book (小红书) for data collection;
Collect data using text mining tools;
Analyse a large corpus of text data using machine learning, sentiment analysis, LLM, etc;
Code major themes from collected data either manually or through automated tools;
Perform literature reviews with a focus on innovations in big data analysis; and
Collaborate on papers, with potential for co-authorship.
Requirements:
Possess a bachelor's or advanced degree in social science, digital humanities, communications, or a quantitative field;
Strong research background, as evidenced in written papers, conference presentations or formal publications;
Possess qualitative and quantitative analytical capability and effective communication skills;
Good command of written English and Chinese; and
It would be advantageous if you have knowledge of or interest in learning about:
Sociology of emotions and/or sentiment analysis;
Analysis of objects and digital images online;
Content analysis of social media, particularly Little Red Book (小红书);
Tourism in China or Asia; or
Nationalism and political emotions
For project and job inquiries, please contact Prof. Gregory Michael FAYARD, Assistant Professor, GSIS (gmfayard@hkbu.edu.hk). Applicants are required to provide their English CV and academic transcript with grade records.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of six months to one year with the possibility of extension.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
