SCHOOL OF CONTINUING EDUCATION
Senior Academic Services Officer (Academic and Student Affairs Section) (Two vacancies) (Ref. No.: 26270156)
The School of Continuing Education, one of the seven Faculties/Schools of the University and a major provider of continuing and professional education in Hong Kong, offers a wide range of full- and part-time programmes at the post-secondary, undergraduate and postgraduate levels for young learners and working adults. It also offers in-house training and short courses to meet the community needs and market demands. Operated on a self-financed basis, the School and its College of International Education currently employ about 400 full-time staff and 550 part-time instructors.
Responsibilities:
The appointees will be required to perform the following major duties at the Academic and Student Affairs Section of the School Registry:
Post 1
Students’ financial subsidies (CEF, FASP, NLSPS and ENLS, etc.);
Maintenance of SEN student records;
Certificate issuance and grade appeal matters;
Co-ordination of Commencement ceremony;
Handle scholarship-related matters, including organising the Scholarship and Award Presentation Ceremony;
Oversee issuance of student ID cards matters;
Provide secretarial support to committees/working groups; and
Handle students’ enquiries.
Post 2
Assist in the School-wide class and examination scheduling exercise (knowledge of “Infosilem Academic” and “Infosilem Exams” would be an added advantage);
Assist in the development and UAT for the new Student Information System;
Handle student records and compile statistics and reports;
Maintenance of student records, such as grade amendment and issuance of academic documents; and
Support the logistic arrangement of programme admission exercise.
Requirements :
A recognised degree with at least 3 years of relevant experience;
