Research Assistant (25260132)
We are seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Research Assistant to support ongoing research projects in the areas of human-AI interaction and customer relationship marketing. The successful candidate will assist with data collection, literature reviews, experimental procedures, and analysis under the supervision of Prof. Kimmy Chan. This is an excellent opportunity for individuals looking to gain hands-on research experience in a dynamic academic/professional environment.
Responsibilities:
Conduct literature reviews and synthesise research findings;
Assist in designing and implementing research methodologies;
Collect, organise, and analyse qualitative/quantitative data;
Collect field work data and engage in training and managing the operation of service robots;
Prepare research materials, reports, and presentations; and
Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with ethical guidelines.
