Collaborating with the Project Coordinator to manage the overall project and facilitate effective implementation;
Managing financial matters, including budget planning, monitoring, and reporting;
Preparing and handling project-related documents, promotional materials, and reports;
Coordinating and supporting the implementation of the aVRINT system in hosting institutions and hospitals;
Organizing and coordinating promotion activities, training sessions, taster workshops, and open seminars for target beneficiaries;
Consolidating user experience feedback, analyzing survey data, and preparing evaluation and pilot testing reports;
Serving as the primary contact point to liaise with project team members, nursing academics, clinical experts, service providers, and vendors to support scenario development as well as software and hardware refinement; and
Assisting in the preparation and dissemination of project outputs, including the e-teaching kit, conference presentations, manuscripts, and the final project report.
Qualifications and Experience Required
Applicants should possess/be:
a bachelor’s degree in healthcare-related discipline, health informatics or computer studies.
experience in manging and coordinating projects;
Familiarity with AI applications in healthcare or education settings (preferred);
Working experience in nursing institution, proficiency in multi-media skills, 3D printing technology or virtual reality technology (preferred);
Have a strong sense of responsibility, good organizational skills, and the ability to work independently as well as in a team; and
Be proficient in both written and spoken Chinese (Cantonese) and English.
Application
Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience.
To apply, please submit your application via system. The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post. Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618.
Application Deadline: 24 August 2026 (Monday)
All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk .
