Major Duties and Responsibilities
The appointee will work under the supervision of Principal Investigator Dr Polly Ma on a research project examining the effectiveness of self-compassion interventions in improving the mental health of transgender and gender diverse individuals, the appointee will be responsible mainly for the following:
Participating in workshop sessions alongside gender minority participants;
Undergoing "train-the-trainer" style briefings to learn the intervention content and facilitation approach;
Providing emotional support and debriefing assistance to participants before, during, and after workshop sessions;
Assisting the project team with on-site logistics and participant engagement as needed; and
Performing any other duties as assigned by the project leader or his/her delegates.
He/she will be normally assigned to work less than 68 hours per four consecutive weeks.
Candidates
Candidates should possess the following qualifications, experience and competence:
A Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Psychology, Social Sciences, Gender Studies, Public Health, or other related disciplines (or equivalent qualifications);
