School of Nursing
Clinical Associate
(Ref. 260206002)
[will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice]
Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders. It ranks 16th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2025). The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community. Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members. We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control.
Duties
The appointee will be required to:
(a) perform teaching and clinical duties in nursing and related areas;
(b) teach pre-registration nursing programmes and supervise students in clinical/field studies;
(c) supervise clinical projects and clinical practicum at undergraduate and postgraduate levels;
(d) contribute to curriculum development and quality improvement of clinical studies;
(e) act as student advisor and counsellor;
(f) coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; and
(g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates.
Qualifications
Applicants should have:
(a) a relevant master’s degree plus not less than four years of post-qualification/post-registration clinical experience in nursing or related areas;
(b) a Certificate of Registration (Part I and/or II) issued by The Nursing Board/Council of Hong Kong;
(c) a valid practicing certificate issued by The Nursing Council of Hong Kong;
(d) a substantial record and reputation as an accomplished clinical teacher;
(e) significant contribution to clinical education innovations and quality improvement initiatives;
(f) demonstrated potential for making substantial contributions to curriculum and pedagogy development and programme management;
(g) a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese; and
(h) effective classroom teaching skills and good communication skills.
Preference will be given to those with clinical experience in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU).
Conditions of Service
A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.
Consideration of applications will commence on 20 February 2026 until the position is filled.
Apply Now
Posting date: 6 February 2026

