SCHOOL OF BUSINESS
OFFICE OF THE DEAN OF BUSINESS
Central Administration Section (CAS)
Assistant Executive Officer (26270078)
The School of Business invites applications for a high-calibre individual to join the Central Administration Section (CAS) of the Dean’s Office of the School of Business, supporting school-wide operations and projects.
Responsibilities:
Provide day-to-day administration support, including handling email inquiries and phone calls, procuring office supplies, conducting classroom and facility inspections, as well as reporting repair and maintenance issues;
Administer the room-booking system and compile usage statistics to prepare reports;
Assist in managing the School’s facilities to support teaching, research, events, and meetings;
Support colleagues in managing the administration and finance matters of research initiatives;
Work closely with team members to deliver School-wide events;
Provide administrative and secretarial services to committees and projects; and
Perform any other duties as assigned.
Requirements:
A recognised bachelor’s degree, with at least two years of relevant work experience, preferably in the tertiary education sector;
A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), and proficiency in IT applications;
