RESEARCH OFFICE
ASSISTANT MANAGER (25260770)
The Research Office (RO) provides central administrative services across grants and funding schemes, research ethics and policy, research committees, infrastructure, and partnerships.
The RO seeks a meticulous team player as Assistant Manager to join the Office.
Responsibilities:
Administer internal research funding schemes, covering infrastructure and publication support, talent awards and student research;
Administer external and government schemes in environment, innovation and health/life sciences (e.g. Environment and Conservation Fund, Green Tech Fund, and Chinese Medicine Development Fund);
Support the full external-grant workflow, from call announcement to submission, change requests and project completion, within performance-pledge timelines;
Support research ethics administration, including clinical and animal research ethics applications, committee/secretariat matters and related coordination;
Liaise with funding bodies and internal units on grant applications and management;
Maintain research grant data and prepare statistical reports; and
Carry out ad hoc tasks as assigned.
Requirements:
A recognised bachelor's degree or above;
A minimum of 5 years of relevant experience, preferably in the higher education sector; experience in research grant administration, RGC and other external schemes and/or research ethics administration is an advantage;
An excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua);
Proficiency in leveraging AI tools to enhance work efficiency and quality;
Good project management and decision-making skills, with the ability to work independently; and
A strong sense of responsibility, meticulous attention to detail, and ability to multitask and handle complexity.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of two years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
