develop and maintain financial models to support feasibility studies, programme planning, knowledge transfer initiatives, self-financing activities and other new opportunities;
work closely with cross-functional teams to ensure accurate, timely and user-oriented financial analysis, forecasts and management reports;
provide proactive recommendations to improve operational workflows, internal controls, policies, guidelines and financial processes from both Finance Office and user-department perspectives;
prepare monthly and quarterly financial and management reports, variance analyses and commentaries for management review and stakeholder discussion;
assist in budgeting, resource planning and financial projections of the University and /or any School, centre, and administrative unit;
support the implementation and enhancement of finance systems, including budgeting, planning and reporting modules, and help users adopt related processes and tools effectively;
liaise with internal and external auditors, tax advisors and any relevant stakeholders; and
implement and promote internal control policies and procedures in accordance with University policy and guidelines.
Applicants Should
be a qualified accountant with a recognised bachelor’s degree in Finance , Accounting, Business Administration or related disciplines;
have at least 8 years of relevant experience in finance and accounting, preferably in the tertiary education sector or Big 4 accounting firms, with solid exposure to business partnering, financial planning and analysis, management reporting, and budgeting;
demonstrate strong business acumen and the ability to engage effectively with academic and administrative units, understand their operational priorities and provide practical financial advice;
possess strong analytical, financial modelling and problem-solving skills, with the ability to present financial information clearly to non-finance stakeholders;
be a proactive team player who can handle duties under tight deadlines, manage multiple priorities and respond effectively to ad hoc requests;
demonstrate strong attention to detail, integrity, professionalism and a service-oriented mindset;
possess strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trust and work collaboratively with stakeholders at different levels; and
be proficient in both written and spoken English and Chinese.
Knowledge of Oracle Fusion would be an advantage.
