fb218c66ae7d96fae2936147.description:
ENTREPRENEURSHIP AND INNOVATION CENTRE
Executive Officer / Assistant Executive Officer (26270113)
Entrepreneurship and Innovation Centre (EIC) is an integral part of the School of Business. EIC is responsible for organising seminars, workshops, competitions, etc. to support the School’s entrepreneurship education.
EIC is seeking self-motivated and responsible individual with good interpersonal skills to fill the position of Executive Officer / Assistant Executive Officer.
Responsibilities:
EIC Operation
Assist in planning and executing EIC projects and activities;
Assist in compiling various kinds of reports and correspondence;
Manage and maintain EIC’s website and social media accounts;
Assist in managing EIC’s data and records;
Event Management
Preparation of promotional materials and newsletters;
Liaise with external and internal stakeholders;
Ensure good event execution and flow;
Branding and Marketing
Design, update and maintain of EIC’s marketing and branding materials;
Promote EIC’s work and positive image to internal and external stakeholders;
Work beyond regular office hours is occasionally required for event support; and
Perform other duties as assigned.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree with at least 2 years of relevant work experience. Some direct exposure in entrepreneurship/innovation or related areas is an advantage;
Effective communication skills with excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua);
Strong interpersonal, organisational and communication skills, the ability to work independently;
Self-motivated with a detailed and analytical mindset;
Good design skills with an eye for details;
Proficiency in computer applications including Microsoft Office software, Chinese word processing, Adobe Illustrator/Adobe Photoshop, and genAI tools; and
Proficiency in updating and maintaining webpages, demonstrating a strong understanding of website management practices.
Shortlisted candidates would be invited for a written test.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed term contract of one year. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to performance review, mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Applicants with less relevant work experience may be considered for the post of Assistant Executive Officer.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications to the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

