Senior Lecturer / Lecturer in Social Work (two posts) (Ref. 260821-03)
Duties
The appointees will be required to:
(a) engage in teaching, programme/curriculum planning and development;
(b) provide academic leadership in teaching-related activities;
(c) contribute to programme validation and quality assurance;
(d) carry out research and scholarly work;
(e) carry out academic and administrative duties;
(f) liaise with industries, professional bodies and organisations, and
(g) perform any other duties as assigned.
The appointees may be required to take up assignments and work outside Hong Kong occasionally.
Qualifications
Applicants should have:
(a) a doctoral degree in related disciplines;
(b) solid relevant teaching, research/scholarship and/or industrial experience;
(c) a Registered Social Worker certificate issued by the Social Workers Registration Board and not less than five years of social work post-degree professional practice experience, preferably specialising in social work in community and macro practice, and/or mental well-being;
(d) excellent teaching performance;
(e) good academic leadership in programme management and development;
(f) a good record of research, and scholarly work or professional engagement, and
(g) good communication and leadership skills.
Applicants with less teaching and/or research/scholarship experience will be considered for the post of Lecturer.
Conditions of Service
An attractive remuneration package will be offered. Initial appointment will be made on a two-year contract.
Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.
﻿ Consideration of applications will commence on 4 September 2026 until the positions are filled.
Posting Date: 21-Aug-2026

